---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${site.name} handles information submitted through this website.`}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      {/* CONFIRM: the owner reviews this privacy policy before launch, then delete this note. The owner must also supply two things the page does not state yet: an effective date ("Last updated ...") and a retention period (how long quote requests and messages are kept). */}
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you send a quote request, a part request or a message, we receive the details you enter (name, email, phone, company, PO or reference number, when you need it, delivery preference, ZIP code, machine model or serial number, project details and the {site.store.enabled ? 'parts or services' : 'part numbers or services'} you add to your request).</p>
      <h2>Your quote list</h2>
      <p>Your quote list is kept in your own browser's storage, on your device, until you send it or clear it. We receive it only when you send the quote form.</p>
      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>This website sets no analytics or advertising cookies and does not track you. Because there is no tracking to turn off, it has nothing to change when your browser sends a "Do Not Track" signal.</p>
      <h2>How it is delivered</h2>
      <p>Form submissions are relayed to our inbox by Web3Forms, a form-processing service. We use the information only to respond to your request.</p>
      <p>The website itself is delivered by Cloudflare, which processes each request, including your IP address, in order to serve the pages.</p>
      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share it only with Web3Forms, to deliver your form to us.</p>
      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>California residents may ask what we hold about them or ask us to delete it. Contact <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or call {site.phone}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
